  Without something visible, this is a library nobody calls. Minimal wiring:

  - [38;5;153mindex.html[39m gains a [1m"Remember me"[0m checkbox and a [1mtheme toggle[0m button, plus a small [38;5;153m<style>[39m block with a
    [38;5;153m[data-theme="dark"][39m rule so the toggle visibly does something. [38;5;153m<script src="app.js">[39m becomes [38;5;153mtype="module"[39m.
  - [38;5;153mapp.js[39m imports [38;5;153mcreatePreferences[39m, and on load pre-fills [38;5;153m#username[39m from [38;5;153mrememberedUsername[39m, checks the box if one is
    stored, and applies [38;5;153mtheme[39m to [38;5;153m<html data-theme>[39m.
  - On successful login (the existing stub's [38;5;153m{ success: true }[39m), stores the username if the box is checked, clears it if
    not.
  - The theme toggle flips and persists [38;5;153mtheme[39m immediately.

  [1mThe password is never stored, read, or persisted — only the username.[0m

  [1m5. Testing[0m

  [38;5;153mnpm test[39m → [38;5;153mnode --test[39m, added to [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m. Tests in [38;5;153mtest/preferences.test.mjs[39m against a Map-backed fake storage:
  defaults on empty store, set/get round-trip, corrupt JSON falls back to defaults, a single invalid stored value falls
  back without affecting siblings, unknown keys throw, invalid values throw, a throwing [38;5;153msetItem[39m returns [38;5;153mfalse[39m instead of
  propagating, and the no-storage in-memory fallback works.

  No new dependencies anywhere.

